        "## ⏰ Part 2: Predefined Libraries for Date & Time\n",
        "\n",
        "Dates are tricky because of leap years, month length differences, and different global formats. Python's `datetime` module makes handling schedules easy!\n",
        "\n",
        "### Key `strftime()` Formatting Codes:\n",
        "* `%B` : Full month name (e.g., `June`)\n",
        "* `%b` : Abbreviated month name (e.g., `Jun`)\n",
        "* `%d` : Day of the month with zero-padding (e.g., `03`)\n",
        "* `%Y` : 4-digit year (e.g., `2026`)\n",
        "* `%A` : Full weekday name (e.g., `Wednesday`)\n",
        "\n"
      ]
    },
